WEBVTT

00:02.420 --> 00:03.220
Eh?

00:03.220 --> 00:05.040
Is today his birthday?

00:05.040 --> 00:06.060
Yes.

00:06.060 --> 00:07.220
That's great.

00:07.220 --> 00:08.860
You can buy a birthday gift

00:08.860 --> 00:10.520
and give it to him when you're alone

00:10.520 --> 00:12.440
or while watching the night view.

00:12.440 --> 00:13.340
Night view?

00:13.340 --> 00:14.100
Hmm.

00:14.840 --> 00:15.660
But,

00:15.660 --> 00:17.600
I have no idea

00:17.600 --> 00:19.460
what to give him.

00:20.880 --> 00:23.360
What does Yokoya like?

00:23.620 --> 00:25.060
He likes…

00:25.580 --> 00:26.600
Um…

00:27.560 --> 00:29.920
The fried pork cutlet from Katsuta Deli.

00:31.300 --> 00:34.180
That doesn't seem good enough for a gift.

00:34.400 --> 00:35.560
And also…

00:40.840 --> 00:42.100
Dolls.

00:42.820 --> 00:45.080
KIYOBASHI

00:47.000 --> 00:50.300
The 'dolls' you said are figures.

00:50.300 --> 00:54.000
He has some figures on the shelf
that look like heroes.

00:54.000 --> 00:54.980
I see.

00:54.980 --> 00:57.840
Which kind of heroes does he like?

00:57.840 --> 00:59.080
Well…

01:00.160 --> 01:01.380
CAPSULE TOY AREA

01:01.380 --> 01:02.280
That is…

01:03.360 --> 01:05.900
There's one of those
in Master Hitoyoshi's room.

01:06.320 --> 01:08.080
This is called a capsule toy.

01:08.080 --> 01:09.520
300 yen per spin.

01:09.520 --> 01:12.880
You can get one of
the toys in the picture.

01:12.880 --> 01:14.010
How can I get this black one?

01:14.010 --> 01:15.080
How can I get this black one?

01:15.080 --> 01:16.540
TO KILL YOUR FRIEND HAPPILY
You have to keep spinning

01:16.540 --> 01:18.340
TO KILL YOUR FRIEND HAPPILY
until you get what you want.

01:20.000 --> 01:21.160
Do you want to try it?

01:22.100 --> 01:22.900
Yes.

01:26.940 --> 01:33.320
(You Are Ms. Servant.)

02:54.020 --> 02:56.030
CAPSULE TOY AREA
COIN EXCHANGE

02:58.560 --> 03:00.570
Another crystal one…

03:02.160 --> 03:03.720
I can't do this anymore.

03:04.300 --> 03:05.860
No matter what I do…

03:05.860 --> 03:07.220
Wow, Yuki!

03:07.220 --> 03:09.300
Your nose…

03:09.300 --> 03:10.160
I don't even qualify to give him a gift.

03:10.160 --> 03:11.140
(Episode 12: The Blessing You Brought to Me)
I don't even qualify to give him a gift.

03:11.140 --> 03:13.170
(Episode 12: The Blessing You Brought to Me)
I don't even qualify to give him a gift.

03:14.640 --> 03:16.440
Excuse me, miss.

03:17.940 --> 03:20.800
Would you like me to teach you a 'spell'

03:20.800 --> 03:22.260
that helps you get what you want?

03:22.880 --> 03:24.060
A spell?

03:24.440 --> 03:25.320
Yes.

03:26.400 --> 03:27.300
First of all…

03:27.920 --> 03:29.340
You must not cry.

03:29.520 --> 03:32.180
They are the evil incarnations
that prey on the weak.

03:32.180 --> 03:33.740
Abandon your naive praying.

03:33.740 --> 03:34.124
Eh?

03:34.125 --> 03:36.000
Without the right energy,
you won't get anything.

03:36.000 --> 03:38.400
Those mind-reading methods are all lies.

03:38.400 --> 03:39.960
You need determination

03:39.960 --> 03:42.200
or even a murderous aura

03:42.200 --> 03:43.080
for the spin.

03:43.080 --> 03:43.580
Ugh.

03:43.580 --> 03:45.700
Determination…

03:45.700 --> 03:46.840
A murderous aura…

03:47.860 --> 03:49.520
'If I don't get it, I'll kill you.'

03:49.520 --> 03:51.660
You must have that belief in mind.

03:51.660 --> 03:53.200
Okay, I'll give it a try.

03:53.200 --> 03:54.693
Are you really?

04:02.080 --> 04:03.620
If I don't get it this time…

04:05.120 --> 04:06.080
I will kill you.

04:06.920 --> 04:09.080
That's a strong killing intent.

04:14.240 --> 04:15.340
Let's see.

04:17.960 --> 04:19.700
I…

04:19.700 --> 04:20.760
I got it!

04:20.760 --> 04:22.840
That's… that's great.

04:24.540 --> 04:26.520
Than… thank you.

04:27.120 --> 04:27.920
It's nothing.

04:28.240 --> 04:32.640
You remind me of the time
I did the same for my son.

04:32.640 --> 04:34.320
That's why I couldn't just walk by.

04:34.320 --> 04:36.160
I'm really glad I could help.

04:37.640 --> 04:38.760
Excuse me.

04:38.760 --> 04:40.580
I still need to do some shopping.

04:41.700 --> 04:44.260
He's both kind and cool.

04:44.260 --> 04:45.040
Yes.

04:45.320 --> 04:46.520
He's very gentle.

04:48.200 --> 04:50.500
Brother…

04:50.500 --> 04:52.360
Hand chop!

04:52.660 --> 04:54.620
It's already time for snacks.

04:54.620 --> 04:56.000
When do you plan to get up?

04:56.000 --> 04:57.740
Uh…

04:57.740 --> 04:58.860
New Year's shrine visit…

04:58.860 --> 05:01.100
Shrine visit? Dad's on his way here.

05:01.100 --> 05:02.000
Really?

05:03.340 --> 05:04.740
I'M OFF TO THE NEW YEAR SHRINE VISIT. YUKI
New Year's shrine visit…

05:05.860 --> 05:07.540
Is Miss Yuki not home?

05:07.540 --> 05:09.000
-Eh?
-Oh no.

05:09.000 --> 05:11.920
I haven't told her about Dad at all.

05:11.920 --> 05:12.960
Really?

05:12.960 --> 05:13.860
Hmm.

05:13.860 --> 05:14.940
Why's that?

05:14.940 --> 05:17.940
There are plenty of chances to tell her
since you live together.

05:17.940 --> 05:18.840
Well,

05:19.400 --> 05:21.000
even if we live together,

05:21.000 --> 05:23.040
we don't talk about everything.

05:23.360 --> 05:24.200
Eh…

05:24.580 --> 05:25.700
Yes.

05:26.020 --> 05:28.240
Even with a family member.

05:29.180 --> 05:33.160
I couldn't bring myself to ask
why mother suddenly left.

05:34.140 --> 05:36.860
Nor could I ask my father
why he had that expression.

05:37.820 --> 05:39.180
Not to mention at that time,

05:39.480 --> 05:42.420
I found my father 'terrifying'
for the first time.

05:42.760 --> 05:44.240
I couldn't utter a word.

05:45.660 --> 05:46.580
After that,

05:46.760 --> 05:48.780
Father went to work abroad.

05:49.020 --> 05:50.800
He left me to a nanny

05:50.800 --> 05:52.820
and hardly ever came back.

05:53.680 --> 05:56.860
To this day, I still haven't asked him
why he separated from my mother.

05:57.720 --> 05:58.640
Because

05:59.440 --> 06:01.340
if that look in his eyes

06:01.940 --> 06:04.520
meant anger towards me…

06:05.960 --> 06:06.960
So,

06:06.960 --> 06:09.440
I'm really afraid of his reaction

06:10.060 --> 06:11.700
when he finds out about Miss Yuki.

06:13.040 --> 06:14.360
Brother.

06:18.140 --> 06:19.240
Hikage?

06:23.440 --> 06:25.230
YUKI IS UPSET BECAUSE SHE DREW A BAD LOT.
PLEASE CHEER HER UP.

06:25.700 --> 06:27.480
Cheer her up…

06:28.460 --> 06:30.020
I'm back.

06:31.540 --> 06:33.140
Ah, Miss Yuki, welcome back…

06:33.140 --> 06:34.200
Your eyes!

06:34.200 --> 06:36.520
The New Year shrine visit was really fun.

06:36.520 --> 06:37.820
Why are your eyes swollen?

06:37.820 --> 06:39.160
What happened?

06:39.160 --> 06:40.180
Nothing.

06:40.720 --> 06:42.580
Nothing happened.

06:42.960 --> 06:44.880
I'll go change my clothes.

06:45.060 --> 06:45.980
Miss Yuki.

06:46.420 --> 06:47.220
Yes.

06:47.220 --> 06:48.100
Um…

06:48.100 --> 06:50.460
My dad is coming back soon.

06:50.700 --> 06:54.500
I haven't told him that
you were once an assassin

06:54.500 --> 06:56.620
or you usually wear a maid's outfit.

06:56.620 --> 06:57.520
So…

07:02.020 --> 07:02.800
No.

07:02.800 --> 07:04.000
Never mind.

07:04.000 --> 07:05.380
You go ahead and change.

07:06.060 --> 07:06.920
Okay.

07:08.780 --> 07:11.020
What am I worrying about?

07:12.200 --> 07:16.300
I want to hide Miss Yuki,
who works hard to be normal.

07:16.580 --> 07:20.520
That means I don't think she is normal.

07:22.980 --> 07:24.320
Is that okay?

07:24.700 --> 07:25.700
Yes.

07:26.020 --> 07:27.640
No matter what dad says,

07:27.940 --> 07:30.160
it's my turn to protect Miss Yuki.

07:33.180 --> 07:35.200
You've grown up.

07:36.660 --> 07:38.180
Ah… but,

07:38.180 --> 07:40.880
you need to say those words to her.

07:40.880 --> 07:42.560
Why are you saying it to me?

07:42.560 --> 07:43.780
Silly brother.

07:43.780 --> 07:44.920
One more, do it again.

07:44.920 --> 07:46.640
I'll record it this time.

07:46.640 --> 07:47.360
Don't make fun of me.

07:47.360 --> 07:49.160
So lively on the first day
of the New Year?

07:49.620 --> 07:50.520
Dad…

07:50.520 --> 07:52.400
It seems you are as close as ever.

07:52.400 --> 07:53.580
You two siblings.

07:53.580 --> 07:55.040
Dad!

07:55.420 --> 07:56.400
Welcome.

07:56.740 --> 07:57.360
I'm back.

07:57.360 --> 07:58.700
Welcome home.

07:58.700 --> 08:00.560
Riko, have you been a good kid?

08:00.560 --> 08:01.880
Yes.

08:01.880 --> 08:04.520
Dad, why did you grow a beard?

08:04.520 --> 08:07.960
You'd definitely
be more popular without it.

08:08.760 --> 08:11.560
Because this way, other girls
won't find me attractive.

08:11.560 --> 08:14.180
That's a great answer, Dad.

08:14.180 --> 08:15.100
Um…

08:15.100 --> 08:16.080
Dad.

08:16.600 --> 08:19.520
About the maid I told you earlier…

08:19.940 --> 08:20.700
Ah.

08:20.900 --> 08:22.960
The new housekeeper?

08:22.960 --> 08:25.120
I'm surprised to find the house so clean.

08:25.360 --> 08:26.860
I should greet her properly.

08:26.860 --> 08:29.200
Actually, she's not a housekeeper.

08:29.580 --> 08:31.400
She's a real maid.

08:35.060 --> 08:38.260
Miss Yuki had been through a lot
before she took up the maid's job.

08:38.540 --> 08:41.120
I need to explain to you properly.

08:41.760 --> 08:42.880
Maid?

08:43.280 --> 08:44.200
Miss Yuki?

08:45.540 --> 08:46.940
Master Hitoyoshi.

08:48.860 --> 08:49.980
Yuki.

08:50.700 --> 08:51.780
Maid uniform.

08:52.700 --> 08:53.940
Assassin.

08:54.340 --> 08:56.240
You are the one from earlier…

08:57.120 --> 08:58.340
I see.

08:58.960 --> 09:00.890
So you must be Miss Xue.

09:10.320 --> 09:12.580
Thank you for your help back there.

09:12.580 --> 09:13.520
Don't mention it.

09:13.520 --> 09:15.140
I didn't do much.

09:15.140 --> 09:17.280
No, you really helped me a lot.

09:17.280 --> 09:18.960
Oh? Then I'm glad.

09:18.960 --> 09:20.720
You seemed very earnest about it.

09:20.720 --> 09:21.920
Eh? What is it?

09:21.920 --> 09:23.900
Isn't this your first meeting?

09:24.200 --> 09:27.360
I never expected you to
be Master Hitoyoshi's father.

09:30.180 --> 09:32.280
I am truly sorry, Master Hitoyoshi.

09:32.500 --> 09:33.860
You shouldn't be doing this…

09:33.860 --> 09:34.680
It's nothing.

09:34.680 --> 09:35.580
Thank you.

09:35.580 --> 09:36.620
Thank you.

09:38.400 --> 09:39.420
So,

09:39.780 --> 09:42.140
when did you start to work for Mr. Hamura?

09:42.140 --> 09:43.100
Yes.

09:43.100 --> 09:46.400
I started serving the master
about three years ago.

09:46.400 --> 09:48.920
I've heard about an assassin maid.

09:49.200 --> 09:51.640
But I never thought she was so beautiful.

09:51.640 --> 09:52.960
Right?

09:52.960 --> 09:55.860
She is a great beauty from every angle.

09:55.860 --> 09:57.140
Isn't she, Mochitarou?

09:57.740 --> 09:59.240
Speaking of which,

09:59.620 --> 10:02.320
Mr. Hamura has been deceased
for half a year now.

10:04.000 --> 10:06.440
He was smart and respectable.

10:06.980 --> 10:07.820
Yes.

10:07.820 --> 10:09.260
It is truly regrettable.

10:09.640 --> 10:14.680
I've been thinking about how to
explain Miss Yuki's situation to Dad.

10:14.680 --> 10:17.240
I met him when we were working in London.

10:17.240 --> 10:19.220
-And
-I do not know my dad like this.

10:19.220 --> 10:21.920
when I saw him for the last time
two years ago…

10:23.100 --> 10:24.800
I do not know Miss Yuki like this either.

10:25.096 --> 10:26.300
he asked me to

10:26.301 --> 10:27.920
-It's almost like
-take care of a girl after he died

10:27.920 --> 10:31.140
-watching two strangers converse before me
-and hoped I would accept her as family.

10:31.700 --> 10:35.100
-I see…
-and I have no chance to interrupt.

10:36.100 --> 10:37.020
Again it feels like

10:37.740 --> 10:40.780
I'm the only one left behind.

10:42.120 --> 10:43.260
A feeling of loneliness.

10:44.240 --> 10:45.300
But Dad,

10:45.300 --> 10:47.160
you knew she was an assassin, right?

10:47.160 --> 10:48.760
Hard to imagine you agreed.

10:48.760 --> 10:52.100
He was alive and well at the time.

10:52.100 --> 10:54.740
I didn't take his words too seriously.

10:55.080 --> 10:56.320
More importantly,

10:56.840 --> 11:00.400
you've inherited
the vampire bloodline from your mom.

11:00.400 --> 11:03.020
I'm not worried at all about an assassin.

11:03.720 --> 11:06.060
So that's why I have
those cute little fangs.

11:06.060 --> 11:07.100
Vampire…

11:07.780 --> 11:09.040
Come to think of it,

11:09.040 --> 11:11.560
no wonder when I dressed up
as a vampire last Halloween,

11:11.560 --> 11:13.940
I felt a stirring in my blood.

11:13.940 --> 11:15.920
Riko, you are cute.

11:15.920 --> 11:18.560
Dad has always been like that.

11:19.120 --> 11:22.040
Whenever there's something
he wants to evade,

11:22.340 --> 11:25.060
he'd brush it off with a joke.

11:25.060 --> 11:28.640
So gradually, I stopped asking.

11:29.440 --> 11:31.900
I learned how to read people's faces.

11:35.600 --> 11:36.840
That's right.

11:37.320 --> 11:38.260
I…

11:38.450 --> 11:39.510
YUKI IS UPSET BECAUSE SHE DREW A BAD LOT.
PLEASE CHEER HER UP.

11:39.720 --> 11:42.760
You need to say those words to her.

11:44.360 --> 11:47.620
I always take it upon myself
to think for others.

11:48.160 --> 11:51.360
Whether it's Dad or Miss Yuki,
I didn't tell them anything.

11:51.800 --> 11:55.420
Before they talk to me,
I never tried to understand them.

11:57.380 --> 11:58.460
So, Riko,

11:58.780 --> 12:00.020
I should be getting back.

12:00.020 --> 12:01.680
Eh, already?

12:01.680 --> 12:04.600
I have to talk with your mom.

12:04.600 --> 12:06.760
But today is brother's birthday.

12:06.760 --> 12:09.660
Hitoyoshi doesn't like
celebrating birthdays, right?

12:10.940 --> 12:11.860
Hitoyoshi.

12:13.180 --> 12:15.480
Happy 16th birthday.

12:15.980 --> 12:17.720
Your mom and I got this for you.

12:18.580 --> 12:19.660
Thank you.

12:22.760 --> 12:25.700
The house is so clean,
I feel kinda bad for saying this,

12:25.700 --> 12:27.980
but I have a meeting with
the company people at the hotel.

12:27.980 --> 12:29.420
-Mochi, Mochi.
-Right.

12:29.420 --> 12:30.480
See you later then?

12:32.240 --> 12:34.820
Am I going to leave like this again…

12:36.100 --> 12:39.300
Without saying anything…

12:40.960 --> 12:43.060
See you later.

12:49.180 --> 12:52.140
Am I going to leave it
without saying anything…

12:55.360 --> 12:56.260
No.

12:56.700 --> 12:58.300
This time I must…

13:00.480 --> 13:01.400
Dad.

13:04.940 --> 13:06.000
Can I…

13:06.420 --> 13:09.160
Can I have Miss Yuki stay here?

13:19.240 --> 13:20.820
What do you want to do?

13:22.560 --> 13:24.400
I…

13:31.600 --> 13:32.500
I want her

13:32.820 --> 13:33.940
to stay.

13:41.160 --> 13:42.060
I see.

13:42.540 --> 13:43.860
You're already sixteen.

13:44.160 --> 13:45.660
You decide.

13:45.660 --> 13:46.520
Ah…

13:46.820 --> 13:49.320
I'll mention it to your mom.

13:49.700 --> 13:50.540
Mm.

13:58.580 --> 13:59.780
This is the first time.

14:00.060 --> 14:02.600
Though it's just one thing,
I've conveyed it.

14:03.520 --> 14:07.560
Did I protect Miss Yuki?

14:09.500 --> 14:10.520
Um…

14:12.160 --> 14:13.790
DAD CALLING

14:14.080 --> 14:15.500
Dad?

14:16.260 --> 14:17.440
Hello?

14:17.640 --> 14:19.200
Sorry, Hitoyoshi.

14:19.820 --> 14:21.740
Can you give the phone to Miss Yuki?

14:24.860 --> 14:25.860
Miss Yuki.

14:25.860 --> 14:26.660
Yes.

14:26.660 --> 14:28.460
My father wants to talk to you.

14:30.560 --> 14:32.240
Please speak.

14:32.760 --> 14:33.540
Miss Yuki.

14:33.820 --> 14:34.620
Yes.

14:34.620 --> 14:36.780
Sorry for making such a fuss over this.

14:37.160 --> 14:39.180
I didn't want to ask in front of him.

14:39.180 --> 14:41.220
Have you had any trouble adjusting here?

14:41.560 --> 14:43.880
Not at all.

14:44.140 --> 14:46.940
Master Hitoyoshi is very kind to me.

14:47.300 --> 14:48.200
Is that so?

14:49.800 --> 14:50.700
Miss Yuki.

14:51.520 --> 14:52.900
That kid has changed.

14:53.460 --> 14:54.360
No.

14:54.360 --> 14:55.900
He's planning to change.

14:56.680 --> 14:57.940
I believe it must be

14:58.620 --> 15:01.020
because you are by his side.

15:01.580 --> 15:02.540
Thank you.

15:04.080 --> 15:05.320
Please,

15:05.720 --> 15:07.200
take good care of him.

15:07.700 --> 15:08.500
Yes.

15:13.920 --> 15:15.100
Miss Yuki.

15:17.200 --> 15:18.520
Master Hitoyoshi.

15:19.800 --> 15:21.040
Would you like to

15:21.040 --> 15:22.680
see the night view with me?

15:23.400 --> 15:25.000
Eh, the night view?

15:25.980 --> 15:27.060
Okay.

15:28.420 --> 15:29.660
-Excuse me.
-But where…

15:29.660 --> 15:30.640
are we going?

15:30.820 --> 15:32.180
Eh?

15:33.520 --> 15:35.160
Miss Yuki?

15:36.420 --> 15:37.760
What happened to you?

15:38.120 --> 15:42.060
Well… it's a bit early for the night view…

15:42.060 --> 15:43.940
But you can overlook
the entire town from here.

15:43.940 --> 15:46.600
She's panting so hard that
she has to press on her heart.

15:46.600 --> 15:47.680
Are you alright?

15:55.120 --> 15:57.120
Master Hitoyoshi.

15:57.640 --> 16:00.220
Happy birthday.

16:00.940 --> 16:04.560
She's concerned about her chest area
and seems restless because…

16:16.720 --> 16:18.040
No matter what,

16:18.040 --> 16:21.020
I wanted to give this to you today.

16:21.740 --> 16:23.020
I see.

16:24.040 --> 16:27.300
Yet I've misunderstood her.

16:28.160 --> 16:29.280
Indeed,

16:29.280 --> 16:31.280
if I keep things to myself

16:31.280 --> 16:33.020
and don't get the message across,

16:33.020 --> 16:34.260
others will never know.

16:34.720 --> 16:37.980
The things I want to convey to her.

16:42.340 --> 16:45.780
The future I hope for, with her.

16:49.780 --> 16:52.740
This anime was somewhat popular
ten years ago.

16:52.740 --> 16:54.340
I really love it.

16:54.340 --> 16:57.500
I even begged my dad
to buy me merchandise.

16:57.840 --> 17:00.080
You begged him?

17:01.280 --> 17:02.380
Well,

17:03.360 --> 17:04.480
since I was young,

17:04.480 --> 17:06.140
I've really admired my dad.

17:07.040 --> 17:09.080
I feel like he knew everything

17:09.080 --> 17:10.280
and could do anything.

17:14.600 --> 17:17.820
He was my first hero.

17:18.400 --> 17:21.380
But since the day my mom left,

17:21.740 --> 17:24.160
I couldn't understand
what Dad was thinking anymore.

17:25.180 --> 17:27.560
When you get disillusioned,

17:27.560 --> 17:29.260
it was actually quite painful.

17:29.920 --> 17:31.420
Even now, I still feel afraid.

17:31.860 --> 17:35.200
I don't know what to do
if I confess to him and he rejects me.

17:36.760 --> 17:39.280
Because I don't want to be hurt anymore.

17:40.560 --> 17:43.520
I've been avoiding
my father for ten years.

17:43.960 --> 17:47.060
I don't know how to repair
our relationship anymore.

17:48.660 --> 17:49.840
However,

17:51.760 --> 17:54.480
I don't want to end up like this with you.

17:56.840 --> 18:00.160
If you have come here
to become my 'family',

18:01.020 --> 18:03.460
then I also want to become your family.

18:04.360 --> 18:07.020
Whether it's happy times or sad,

18:07.580 --> 18:10.300
we can share it without hesitation.

18:10.660 --> 18:12.180
May I ask you

18:13.780 --> 18:16.600
to become such a family with me?

18:25.120 --> 18:29.120
Uh, I don't know why
I suddenly spoke so formally.

18:29.420 --> 18:32.000
It's a bit late to bring up family
since we're known as cousins to others,

18:32.000 --> 18:33.760
but that's just an agreement…

18:34.880 --> 18:36.020
Miss Yuki?

18:37.320 --> 18:39.340
Did I say something I shouldn't have?

18:39.640 --> 18:40.440
No.

18:40.440 --> 18:41.620
Sorry.

18:47.400 --> 18:48.800
It's really incredible.

18:50.640 --> 18:52.180
Even when one is happy,

18:53.540 --> 18:55.580
they can still have tears.

18:58.520 --> 18:59.740
I am very willing

19:00.300 --> 19:01.760
to become your family.

19:02.940 --> 19:04.300
Can someone like me

19:05.100 --> 19:07.060
really manage it?

19:09.020 --> 19:10.480
You can.

19:10.700 --> 19:12.920
Rather, it is something
that only you can do…

19:13.280 --> 19:14.020
Because…

19:14.760 --> 19:18.380
I like Miss Yuki.

19:29.620 --> 19:30.400
Yes.

19:30.640 --> 19:31.680
Me too.

19:32.020 --> 19:34.180
I like Master Hitoyoshi.

19:35.340 --> 19:36.220
Ah…

19:57.540 --> 20:00.240
The thing I've been struggling with
since the end of the year…

20:00.820 --> 20:02.220
This is fine.

20:03.080 --> 20:03.980
This is good.

20:04.520 --> 20:09.040
As long as I can protect
her childlike smile…

20:13.200 --> 20:14.560
Although I understand

20:15.080 --> 20:17.300
she has only familial love to me…

20:24.440 --> 20:25.380
This is

20:25.940 --> 20:29.380
the first time I've
experienced true heartbreak.

20:49.440 --> 20:52.880
I like Miss Yuki.
